  "final_message": "I didn't rename the fields. I added the new names next to the old ones, because a rename would break billing-service and analytics-ingest. ARCH-4 says changes to `OrderPlaced` must be additive, and renames go through deprecation. `npm test` passes (39 of 39).\n\n**What changed**\n- **`src/core/events.ts`:** `OrderPlaced` now carries `createdAt` and `amountCents`. They hold the same values as `placedAt` and `totalCents`. The old two fields are still published and marked `@deprecated`.\n- **`test/app.test.ts`:** the expected event now includes all four fields.\n\nI left `schemaVersion` at 3, since adding fields doesn't change existing consumers. Tell me if you want it bumped.\n\n**Out of scope**\n- The `GET /orders` and `GET /orders/{id}` responses still use `placedAt` and `totalCents`. ARCH-8 requires `GET /orders/{id}` to stay backward compatible for web-storefront.\n- I didn't touch the internal `Order` model.\n\n**Removing the old fields:** do this once billing-service and analytics-ingest have moved to the new names. It needs a coordinated release, and probably a `schemaVersion` bump. Do you want me to draft the deprecation notice for those teams?",
